# 1. CORE PROCUREMENT ARCHITECTURE

Establish two clearly differentiated procurement mechanisms.

## A. INVENTORY PURCHASE REQUISITION

Used when the primary procurement requirement is inventory or material.

Supports:
- Inventory item lines.
- Item quantities and UOM.
- Unit price.
- Warehouse selection.
- Delivery schedules.
- Inventory-linked Charge Items.
- Header-level Charge Items.
- Line-level Charge Items.
- Landed cost calculation.

Examples:

Raw Material Purchase:
- Material: ₹30,000
- Freight: ₹3,000
- Loading: ₹1,000
- Insurance: ₹500

These additional expenses belong to the inventory procurement transaction.

They must be recorded as Charge Items, not as independent Expense PR lines.

## B. EXPENSE PURCHASE REQUISITION

Introduce a new PR Type:

EXPENSE – Expense Purchase Requisition.

Used when the requirement is an independent expense or service and is not an additional cost associated with an inventory purchase.

Examples:
- Consultancy.
- Professional Fees.
- Legal Fees.
- Audit Fees.
- Office Rent.
- Software Subscription.
- Training.
- Independent Maintenance Services.
- Facility Management.
- Administrative Services.
- Other approved operational expenses.

An Expense PR must not require inventory item lines.

It must support multiple independent expense/service lines.

## C. CLASSIFICATION RULE – MANDATORY

Apply the following business rule:

If an expense is directly associated with inventory procurement, classify it as a Charge Item.

If an expense is independent of inventory procurement, classify it under EXPENSE PR.

Examples:

| Expense | Classification |
|---|---|
| Freight for purchased raw material | Charge Item |
| Loading purchased material | Charge Item |
| Insurance for purchased shipment | Charge Item |
| Packing for purchased material | Charge Item |
| Independent transportation contract | EXPENSE PR |
| Annual consultancy fees | EXPENSE PR |
| Software subscription | EXPENSE PR |
| Office rent | EXPENSE PR |
| Independent maintenance service | EXPENSE PR |

Do not classify expenses using their names alone.

Use the business purpose and relationship to the inventory procurement transaction.

Prevent duplicate recording of the same expense as both a Charge Item and an independent Expense PR.

