# 12. SAP BUSINESS ONE 10.0 HANA INTEGRATION

Koshit is the procurement governance and workflow platform.

SAP Business One is the ERP system for the purchasing transactions assigned to it.

Use the existing SAP Business One Service Layer integration.

Never write directly to SAP HANA application tables.

## 12.1 Inventory PR Integration

For approved inventory PRs:

- Generate SAP Item-type Purchase Requests.
- Map inventory item codes.
- Map quantities and UOM.
- Map warehouse information.
- Map delivery dates.
- Preserve Koshit PR and line references.

Charge Items must remain associated with the inventory procurement transaction.

At the subsequent SAP purchasing document stage:

- Map eligible header-level charges to SAP document-level Additional Expenses.
- Map eligible line-level charges to SAP row-level Additional Expenses.
- Validate SAP expense codes.
- Validate tax mappings.
- Validate account determination.
- Prevent duplicate posting.

Do not assume every Charge Item is automatically available as an expense in every SAP document type.

Verify the actual installed SAP B1 version, patch level and Service Layer metadata before implementing the mappings.

## 12.2 EXPENSE PR Integration

For approved EXPENSE PRs:

- Generate SAP Service-type Purchase Requests.
- Map expense descriptions and supported service purchasing information.
- Validate configured service purchasing requirements.
- Validate SAP expense account mappings.
- Validate tax mappings.
- Preserve vendor and currency information where applicable.
- Preserve the Koshit Expense PR reference.

Do not create dummy inventory items.

Do not convert every expense into an inventory-linked Additional Expense.

## 12.3 SAP Expense and Account Mapping

Maintain approved mappings between:

Koshit Expense Category
→ SAP Service Purchasing Information
→ SAP Expense/Account Determination
→ Applicable Tax Configuration.

The actual SAP mapping must be validated against the installed system.

Do not fabricate account codes or tax codes.

## 12.4 SAP Document Conversion

During the subsequent Purchase Order conversion process:

- Preserve the original Koshit PR reference.
- Preserve Charge Item references.
- Apply eligible document-level and line-level Additional Expenses.
- Respect supplier and purchasing configuration.
- Prevent duplicate expense posting.
- Maintain SAP document references.

Do not automatically create separate Purchase Orders for every expense.

Respect the existing procurement and supplier selection process.

